## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical security thinking for a data ingestion flow involving Databricks, focusing on validation, secure storage, and auditable operations.

## Key Concepts

- Input validation (MIME type, file signatures, allowed extensions)
- Secure storage with encryption and least-privilege IAM
- Service-to-service authentication to Databricks API
- Auditability and key rotation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example server-side validation (pseudo)
const allowedExt = '.csv';
if (!file.name.endsWith(allowedExt) || mimeType !== 'text/csv') {
  throw new Error('Unsupported file');
}
// proceed to store and trigger Databricks job
```

